hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1341","Abu Musa told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-A’mash told us, Salam bin Junada told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim On the authority of Alqamah, they said: A man came to Omar while he was standing at Arafat, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful, I came from Kufa and left there a man who dictated He learned the Qur’an by heart, so Omar became angry and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was still staying with Abu Bakr tonight. Such is the matter among the affairs of the Muslims.”"
"1342","Abu Bakr said: The news of Abdullah bin Amr, of this kind, was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, telling us about the Children of Israel. Until the morning he does not stand there except for the greatest prayer.” Bundar told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Hassan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, H and he told us Bundar, Affan told us, Abu Hilal told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Hassan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn: on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He acknowledged the same. Abu Bakr said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to speak to them after the evening meal about the Children of Israel, so that they might learn from what had befallen them. The punishment in this world is in addition to the punishment God has prepared for them in the Hereafter when they disobeyed their messengers and did not believe. It is permissible for a person to narrate all He does not know that the listener will benefit from the matter of his religion after the evening meal, since the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to contemplate the matter after the evening prayer. Of the affairs of the Muslims, which is due to their benefit, sooner or later, in religious and worldly matters, and he used to tell his companions about the Children of Israel so that they might benefit. With his hadith, his action, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, indicates that it is disliked to talk after dinner about something that has no benefit in religion or the world, and it is dangerous. I think that he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, disliked working with a tan, because that discouraged him from praying the night prayers, because if he worked at the beginning of the night Because of the darkness, sleep became difficult for him at the end of the night, so he did not wake up, and if he did wake up, he did not have the energy to get up."
